---
<Layout title="Data and code | OpenIE Research" description="Where each paper's results live in the public experiments and reference repositories.">
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl text-brand-white">Data and code</h1>
    <div class="mt-5 glass-card p-5 border border-brand-amber/35 bg-brand-amber/[0.04]">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-amber mb-2">In Plain Words · How to Read These Receipts</p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-light leading-relaxed m-0">
        Every study on this site links to open code, test inputs, and cryptographic checksums so anyone can re-run our numbers without trusting us on faith. To keep energy comparisons honest, we never mix four separate ways of recording energy: <code class="text-emerald-300">measured_j</code> comes from a physical wire sensor clipped across a circuit board rail, <code class="text-brand-cyan">reported_j</code> comes from a processor's built-in software counter, <code class="text-brand-amber">est_j</code> is a datasheet or math formula estimate, and <code class="text-brand-gray">unmetered</code> means no power meter was attached.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2.5">
      <a href="/blueprint/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-amber border border-brand-amber/40 bg-brand-amber/10 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-amber/20">
        Planetary Media Blueprint v1.0 · 29 Voiced / 50 Captioned →
      </a>
      <a href="/coverage.json" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-emerald-300 border border-emerald-400/40 bg-emerald-500/10 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-emerald-500/20">
        Canonical Coverage JSON (/coverage.json)
      </a>
      <a href="/sourcesheets/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-cyan border border-brand-cyan/40 bg-brand-cyan/10 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-cyan/20">
        29 [G0–G12] Source Sheets
      </a>
      <a href="/media/tv/planetary-15s/v1-media-manifest.json" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate border border-brand-border px-3 py-1.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:text-brand-white">
        1,054-Variant [G6] Whisper-Turbo Manifest
      </a>
      <a href="/glossary/concepts.json" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate border border-brand-border px-3 py-1.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:text-brand-white">
        38 Mulberry+Tawasol AAC Concepts
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">The reproducible material for these studies lives in <a href="https://github.com/openIE-dev/openie-research-experiments">github.com/openIE-dev/openie-research-experiments</a> and companion repositories under <a href="https://github.com/openIE-dev">github.com/openIE-dev</a> (<a href="https://github.com/openIE-dev/rce">rce</a>, <a href="https://github.com/openIE-dev/rce-vc">rce-vc</a>, <a href="https://github.com/openIE-dev/deterministic-null">deterministic-null</a>, and <a href="https://github.com/openIE-dev/lut-adapt-ai">lut-adapt-ai</a>): preregistrations with SHA-256 and BLAKE3 digests, scripts, Lean 4 proof packages, CAD/ECAD hardware files, results, Ed25519-signed receipts (<code>Signed Provenance · Self-Checked</code>), a repository-wide <code>CHECKSUMS.sha256</code>, and pinned references for large corpora (<code>CORPORA.md</code>). Code is Apache-2.0 and data is CC BY 4.0 (metadata and captions CC0-1.0). Energy labels obey strict orthogonality (<code>measured_j ⊥ reported_j ⊥ est_j ⊥ unmetered</code>): <code>est_j</code> is an analytical estimate, <code>reported_j</code> an operating-system or on-chip counter, and <code>measured_j</code> a physical sensor reading on a named hardware rail. Physical current-shunt <code>measured_j</code> readings are filed across Metered Commit Gates (AMD Kria KV260 TI INA260 rows in Section I.4.9: seed freerun in watts, inconclusive +0.0098 W / 98.0 pJ per seed cycle halt-versus-run delta, and 11,428 pJ per gate cycle on the gate fabric), the Satiation Benchmark Harness, The Communication Tool Avalanche (CTA-E4 and CTA-E5), Downward LUT6 Compilation (Claims LA-24 through LA-70 plus Kits 4 and 5), From Ephemeral Inference to Compiled Agency (<code>@ 6a22dee</code> Oct–Nov 2026 6-model SOTA shunt panel across KV260 INA260 and Jetson AGX Thor INA3221/INA238), and the Planetary Research Media Blueprint v1.0 production shunt kit (<code>@ a9de8d8</code> <code>kits/planetary-media-joule/</code> across KV260 INA260 and Thor INA238/INA3221, with shared-host windows exceeding Falsifier 6 drift flagged and net deltas withheld). On-chip <code>reported_j</code> receipts (Apple Silicon IOReport / proc_pid_rusage, Linux x86-64 RAPL, and Windows 11 NVML) are filed for the Reality Code Engine, RCE-VC, RCE-JEPA (H2, H15, FormJEPA-v1, FormEBM-v2, and FormEBM-v3), RCE Compile (E4-Energy, E4-Prelude, and E5-Scale), Deterministic Null, the Satiation Benchmark Harness, The Communication Tool Avalanche (CTA-E1 to CTA-E5), Downward LUT6 Compilation, From Ephemeral Inference to Compiled Agency, Planetary Media Blueprint v1.0, Writing a Game Once (GE-H1 and GE-H5), and "AI" Reads Human, while <code>measured_j</code> remains empty across all software-only and simulated hardware runs.</p>
    {groups.map((g) => (
      <section id={g.id} class="mt-10">
        {g.aliases.map((a) => <div id={a} aria-hidden="true"></div>)}
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl text-brand-white"><a href={g.paper}>{g.title}</a></h2>
        <table class="mt-3 w-full font-body text-sm text-brand-slate">
          <thead><tr><th class="text-left pr-4">Result</th><th class="text-left pr-4">Repository or artifact path</th><th class="text-left">Contents</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>{g.rows.map(([r, p, c]) => (<tr><td class="pr-4 py-1 align-top">{r}</td><td class="pr-4 py-1 align-top">{p ? <a href={hrefOf(p)}><code>{labelOf(p)}</code></a> : 'n/a'}</td><td class="py-1 align-top">{c}</td></tr>))}</tbody>
        </table>
      </section>
    ))}
  </main>
</Layout>
